From 768f64a308a8c1c10994622369c65d4716eff794 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:56:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] fix(project): load pre-v59 meshes as "fidelity unknown"
 and refuse them by name until re-imported

A project saved before #911 recorded no mesh fidelity, so a STEP model
its import kept coarser than promised loaded as full fidelity with no
re-check. Re-measuring on load is impossible (the chord is measured
against the B-rep; the file keeps only facets), and a v58 file cannot
tell a pre-#911 save from a later fine one, nor STEP from STL.

- PROJECT_VERSION 59. Loading an older file marks every mesh without a
  recorded chord (models, fixtures, from-model stock copies) "fidelity
  unknown", with one load note each (project::fidelity_migrate). A
  recorded coarse_mm is kept.
- The mark is the sentinel chord model_fidelity::UNKNOWN_MM on the
  existing ReducedFidelity component, so it rides every copy, clone,
  undo and save path the flag rides. The gate refuses every operation
  judged against it by name, an unknown part refuses the program verdict,
  an unknown fixture refuses through its own gate line; the sim and the
  eye judge nothing. Model page / MCP / script say "Fidelity unknown".
- Saved as "fidelity_unknown": true (never a chord number); both keys on
  one row is corrupt. Only a fresh import clears it.
- examples/first-part and the microARC kit project (exact OBJ / code
  meshes) re-stamped v59.

Decision in docs/decisions/1056-fidelity-unknown.md.

Fixes #1056

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
